pub fn replace_at_token(&mut self, at_col: usize, value: &str) {
    let line = self.lines[self.row].clone();
    let chars: Vec<char> = line.chars().collect();
    let cursor_col = self.col.min(chars.len());
    let prefix: String = chars[..at_col].iter().collect();
    let suffix: String = chars[cursor_col..].iter().collect();
    self.push_undo();
    self.lines[self.row] = format!("{prefix}{value}{suffix}");
    self.col = at_col + value.chars().count();
}
```

`at_col` is the position of `@`. `cursor_col` is where the cursor is (after the query). So the span `[at_col, cursor_col)` is `@query`. Replacing with `value` puts the value in place of `@query`.

So if I call `replace_at_token(at_col, &query)`, it replaces `@query` with just `query`, effectively removing the `@`. The cursor would be at `at_col + query.len()`. That's clean.

